From 859be047fcd65172b3dde61758977684946f475e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Akhil <akhile76@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:28:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] av1: make Chrome's VA-API AV1 decode work on AVD

Chrome's AV1 path differs from FFmpeg's in ways the bridge did not handle:
- it does not fill width/height_in_sbs_minus_1 when uniform_tile_spacing_flag
  is set, so derive the tile geometry from the frame size and log2 tile counts;
- buffer ordering differs (slice data may precede its parameters);
- on AVD, queue each AV1 frame at EndPicture, once all tiles have arrived.

Tested on MacBook Air M4 (J713, AVD): FFmpeg hardware decode byte-exact
against libdav1d (360p, 1080p, end of stream); Chrome 156 WebCodecs and
<video> playback on VaapiVideoDecoder. Host tests: meson test.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Akhil <akhile76@gmail.com>
